  "content": {
    "id": "p51-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Let $P(x)=x^3+ax^2+9x+b$. It is given that $x-2$ is a factor of $P(x)$, and when divided by $x+1$ the remainder is $-18$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p51-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the value of $a$ and $b$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=-6$, $b=-2$.",
          "worked": "By the factor and remainder theorems, $P(2)=0$ and $P(-1)=-18$:\n$$\\begin{align*}8+4a+18+b&=0\\\\4a+b&=-26\\\\-1+a-9+b&=-18\\\\a+b&=-8\\\\3a&=-18\\\\a&=-6\\\\b&=-8-(-6)\\\\b&=-2.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Solve $P(x)=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2$, $x=2+\\sqrt3$ or $x=2-\\sqrt3$.",
          "worked": "Using the known factor $x-2$,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=x^3-6x^2+9x-2\\\\P(x)&=(x-2)(x^2-4x+1).\n\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x=2$ or\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-4x+1&=0\\\\(x-2)^2&=3\\\\x-2&=\\pm\\sqrt3\\\\x&=2\\pm\\sqrt3.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe roots are $2$, $2+\\sqrt3$ and $2-\\sqrt3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      }
    ]
  },
